# 强制 shell 脚本以 LF 行尾检出。
#
# 背景：Windows 上 core.autocrlf=true，工作区里的 *.sh 全是 CRLF
# （git ls-files --eol "*.sh" → i/lf w/crlf attr/）。
# 从 Windows 工作区手工拷到 Linux 的脚本，第一行就崩：
#   line 47: syntax error near unexpected token $'in\r''
#   set: pipefail\r: invalid option name
#
# 服务器 git clone 出来本来就是 LF，所以仓库自带脚本没事，
# 出事的是从 Windows 手工拷过去的。
* text=auto
*.sh text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf

# Windows batch files and the WinSW config must stay CRLF on checkout.
#
# Why this is explicit: `deploy\` held the service's whole launch chain
# (start-backend-service.cmd, release-pid-switch.cmd, CowAgentBackend.xml)
# and it was an UNTRACKED directory -- so a `git clean` (or any tool that
# prunes untracked files) deleted the service's launch chain and the
# service could not start again. A .cmd with LF endings still runs under
# cmd.exe, but a .cmd with mixed endings breaks on the `for /f` line, and
# the XML is read by WinSW's own parser. Pinning the line endings removes
# the question instead of leaving it to chance.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.xml text eol=crlf
*.py text eol=lf
